# C++ Simulation Core

Canonical guidance: `docs/engineering/cpp.md`. Runtime boundary: `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`. Determinism/model semantics: `docs/MODELING.md`.

`src/sim` is the only authoritative world and `src/sim` + `src/protocol` remain Godot-free.

Do:
- semantic intents/commands, not desired-state setters;
- RAII and explicit ownership;
- `std::expected`/typed results for ordinary gameplay failure;
- one explicit seeded RNG state;
- integer/scaled load-bearing domain values by default;
- deterministic iteration/order where outcome depends on order;
- concrete types until a real variation point exists.

Do not:
- include godot-cpp/Godot headers;
- use frame delta or wall clock as simulation time;
- use hidden/system RNG;
- use `nlohmann::json` as live domain state;
- add ECS/job/service-locator frameworks speculatively;
- make exceptions the normal “not enough gold” channel.

Read current headers/tests before naming an API.
